ExLlamaV3 -- https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3
MIT licence, (c) 2025 Turboderp
================================================================================

The EXL3 on-disk format is defined by ExLlamaV3, so the code that decodes it
must match it exactly. These files are vendored from, or follow the structure
of, ExLlamaV3 and carry per-file attribution:

  vllm_exl3/csrc/exl3_dq.cuh        vendored -- trellis dequantisation
  vllm_exl3/csrc/exl3_codebook.cuh  vendored -- procedural codebooks (3inst/mcg/mul1)
  vllm_exl3/csrc/exl3_common.cuh    mma fragment layout and decoders follow it
  vllm_exl3/csrc/exl3_had.cuh       structure follows its hadamard_inner.cuh

ExLlamaV3 is also imported by bench/bench_gemm.py and
bench/bench_vs_spark_fat_gemm.py as a comparison baseline. It is not a runtime
dependency of the plugin.

